        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Barn Door Cost",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/barn-door-cost/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a barn door cost installed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost guides disagree but cluster in the same region. HomeAdvisor gives an average of about $1,800 with a normal range of $1,350 to $5,000; Fixr gives a national average of $1,658; HomeGuide puts installed doors at $400 to $3,400 or more. Where you land depends on the slab material, the hardware, any wall work and who installs it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much is barn door hardware?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Fixr lists standard kits with a track at $42 to $447, HomeAdvisor gives $50 to $500 for basic sets, and HomeGuide puts track kits at $100 to $300 or more. Custom or automated hardware costs considerably more: Fixr gives $600 to $1,200 or more, and HomeAdvisor says it can add up to $1,500."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does barn door installation labour cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "HomeGuide quotes $100 to $1,000, Fixr $308 to $984, and HomeAdvisor and Angi $300 to $2,000. HomeAdvisor describes labour as roughly 30 to 50 percent of the total. Heavier doors, header boards, removing an old door and electrical work in the door's path all push labour towards the top."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it cheaper to install a barn door yourself?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, substantially. Fixr's budget tier of $150 to $500 assumes a big-box kit hung by the homeowner. You need to find studs, fit a level header board and lift the door onto the track with a helper. Fixr notes doors can weigh 44 to 150 pounds, so heavy slabs are best left to two people or a pro."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much do double barn doors cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "HomeAdvisor puts an installed double barn door at $500 to $3,400, compared with $200 to $1,600 for a single. HomeGuide gives $800 to $2,800 for a pair, and Angi says doubles can occasionally exceed $6,000. Pairs need twice the hardware, a long level track and clear wall on both sides."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a header board for a barn door?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually. The track carries a heavy moving load that must reach the framing, and studs rarely line up with the track's holes. A header board fixed across several studs solves that. HomeGuide lists one at $200 to $500 when a contractor fits it; doing it yourself costs mainly the lumber and screws."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are barn doors cheaper than regular doors?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not automatically. A barn door needs a slab larger than the opening, a separate hardware kit and often a header board, none of which a hinged door requires, so the total adds up faster than the door price suggests. Its real saving is space: no swing clearance and no wall to open up, which matters most in tight rooms."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
  ],
};
