        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A barn door's cost is a stack: the slab, the hardware, the header and wall work, the finishing and the labour. Published guides put the installed total anywhere from a few hundred dollars for a self-hung pine kit to several thousand for custom hardwood on custom hardware, with national averages in the region of $1,600 to $1,800.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best value is almost always in good hardware and a solid mounting rather than an expensive slab. Price each line separately, insist on itemised quotes, and leave room in the budget for the wall work and finishing that headline prices so often leave out.
          </p>
        </div>

